1
00:03:39,230 --> 00:03:45,230
Discover a place that will never leave you, and a
friendship that will change you forever.

2
00:07:18,461 --> 00:07:24,461
Bridge to Terabithia is a adventure, drama, family film directed by Gábor Csupó.

3
00:10:57,692 --> 00:11:03,692
Jesse Aarons trained all summer to become the fastest runner in school.

4
00:14:36,923 --> 00:14:42,923
So he's very upset when newcomer Leslie Burke outruns him and everyone else.

5
00:18:16,153 --> 00:18:22,153
Despite this and other differences including that she's rich, he's poor, she's a
city girl, and he's a country boy the two become fast friends.

6
00:21:55,384 --> 00:22:01,384
Together they create Terabithia, a land of monsters, trolls,
ogres, and giants where they rule as king and queen.

7
00:25:34,615 --> 00:25:40,615
Jess Aarons, played by Josh Hutcherson.

8
00:29:13,846 --> 00:29:19,846
Leslie Burke, played by AnnaSophia Robb.

9
00:32:53,076 --> 00:32:59,076
Ms. Edmunds, played by Zooey Deschanel.

10
00:36:32,307 --> 00:36:38,307
Jack Aarons, played by Robert Patrick.

11
00:40:11,538 --> 00:40:17,538
May Belle Aarons, played by Bailee Madison.

12
00:43:50,769 --> 00:43:56,769
Mary Aarons, played by Kate Butler.

13
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Bridge to Terabithia is a 2007 American fantasy drama film directed by Gábor
Csupó (in his directorial debut) from a screenplay by David L.

14
00:51:09,230 --> 00:51:15,230
Paterson and Jeff Stockwell.

15
00:54:48,461 --> 00:54:54,461
It is based on the 1977 novel of the same name by Katherine Paterson and stars Josh
Hutcherson, AnnaSophia Robb, Zooey Deschanel, and Robert Patrick.

16
00:58:27,692 --> 00:58:33,692
In the film, adolescent children Jess Aarons (Hutcherson) and Leslie Burke (Robb) create "Terabithia", a fantasy
world, which they use to cope with their troubled reality and spend their free time together.

17
01:02:06,923 --> 01:02:12,923
The original novel was based on events from the childhood of Paterson's son, who went on to write the film's
screenplay; Csupó was hired in late 2005, and the rest of the main cast was rounded out soon after.

18
01:05:46,153 --> 01:05:52,153
Principal photography began in February 2006 and lasted
until that April, taking place in Auckland.

19
01:09:25,384 --> 01:09:31,384
This was the last film for 71-year-old cinematographer Michael Chapman, who
followed through with his planned retirement thereafter.

20
01:13:04,615 --> 01:13:10,615
Bridge to Terabithia was released in the United States on
February 16, 2007, by Buena Vista Pictures.

21
01:16:43,846 --> 01:16:49,846
It received positive reviews from critics, with praise for its visuals,
cast performances, and faithfulness to the source material.

22
01:20:23,076 --> 01:20:29,076
The film grossed $137.6 million worldwide.

23
01:24:02,307 --> 01:24:08,307
At the 29th Young Artist Awards, the film won all
five awards for which it was nominated.

24
01:27:41,538 --> 01:27:47,538
The film explores themes of friendship, sibling
relationship, bullying, neighbor, school.

25
01:31:20,769 --> 01:31:26,769
The tone is emotional.
